KG42.register("nodes-d5f3009c8264a33d8ca3e8f6",{"id":"COMP-bebd346528bbcf18","code":"PRC011","label":"Shared-storage pricing and publication maximizing buyers' average savings","definition":"The auctioneer, incorporating the RU supply response, selects and publishes the unit shared energy storage price p_t within [p_t^min,p_t^max] to maximize the SFC average cost saving Z=[Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m−p_t)/(K−1)]Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i.","layer":"L6","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: the unit auction price of the shared resource","Core operation: incorporating the autonomous supply response, maximize the buyers' average cost saving within the allowed interval","Output: the auction price p_t used for demand response and payments"]},"exclusions":["p_t^min is what the source calls the Vickrey price, namely the second-highest reserve price among the RU participants; p_t^max is its highest reserve price","Equation (12) reports p_t^*=[(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}1/(2α_i))(Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}a_m)+Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}r_i(K−1)/(2α_i)]/[Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}(K−1)/α_i]","Algorithm 1 searches over the price interval, uses the RU bounded best response to calculate Z, and records the price when Z≥Z*; it is retained separately from equation (12)","Final pricing in the payment rule is executed after the group is determined; the earlier determination of the price upper bound and the time-slot-by-time-slot implementation scope are retained"],"members":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"70bc095c02578bf031b0d54ba69d5113bf40e26156d0d083a18baa255d2a6d9d","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. | Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1. | Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. | Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. | Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g04-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"39afd20ea0ea72205a9a8a085e4da4716b0ead9015ac1c00c330d489bd6248a9","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The auction price is the price SFC customers must pay RU owners for sharing their ES devices. Scope: The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"5419cc826592f82522f0bb04ae5e378cdd735affdcb7cd0978f11399b95e55e0","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. State-of-the-Art","anchor_text":"ge revenues for stakeholders [28], [29]. However, one similar- or- ity among most of the above menti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"the proposed modiﬁed auction scheme studied in Section IV 0) can be adopted in each time slot t = 1,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"er- nality properties, as we will see later, which are desirable in he any mechanism that adopts auc","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, the proposed auction process, as shown in Fig. 2, consists of three elements: 1) Owner: The RUs in set $\\mathcal{N}$, which own the ES devices, and expect to earn some economic benefits, e.g., through maximizing a utility function, by letting the SFCs to share some fraction of their ES spaces. 2) Customer: The SFCs in set $\\mathcal{M}$, which are in need of ESs in order to store some excess electricity at a particular time of the day. The SFCs offer the RUs a price with a view to jointly owning some fraction of their ES devices. 3) Auctioneer: A third party (e.g., estate or building manager), which controls the auction process between the owners and the customers according to some predefined rules.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"To this end, the proposed auction process, as shown in Fig. 2, consists of three elements: 1) Owner: The RUs in set $\\mathcal{N}$, which own the ES devices, and expect to earn some economic benefits, e.g., through maximizing a utility function, by letting the SFCs to share some fraction of their ES spaces. 2) Customer: The SFCs in set $\\mathcal{M}$, which are in need of ESs in order to store some excess electricity at a particular time of the day. The SFCs offer the RUs a price with a view to jointly owning some fraction of their ES devices. 3) Auctioneer: A third party (e.g., estate or building manager), which controls the auction process between the owners and the customers according to some predefined rules."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E36","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as pmint hereinafter. ed However, we note that this secon","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if $p_t$ is set to $p_t = p_t^{\\max}$, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between $p_t^{\\max}$ and $p_t^{\\min}$. To do so, we propose a scheme for deciding on both the auction price $p_t$ and the amount of ESs $x_i$ that RUs will put into the market for sharing according to $p_t$. In particular, we propose a Stackelberg game between the auctioneer, which decides on the auction price $p_t$ to maximize the average cost savings to the SFCs as well as satisfying their desirable needs of ESs, and the RUs, which decide on the vector containing the amounts of ES $\\mathbf{x} = [x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{J-1}]$ that they would like to put into the market for sharing such that their benefits are maximized.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if $p_t$ is set to $p_t = p_t^{\\max}$, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between $p_t^{\\max}$ and $p_t^{\\min}$. To do so, we propose a scheme for deciding on both the auction price $p_t$ and the amount of ESs $x_i$ that RUs will put into the market for sharing according to $p_t$. In particular, we propose a Stackelberg game between the auctioneer, which decides on the auction price $p_t$ to maximize the average cost savings to the SFCs as well as satisfying their desirable needs of ESs, and the RUs, which decide on the vector containing the amounts of ES $\\mathbf{x} = [x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{J-1}]$ that they would like to put into the market for sharing such that their benefits are maximized."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p12-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Case Study","anchor_text":"p gy y his have enough ES to share with the SFC. However, the ES to ed share in time slot 4 stems fr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}].","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. System Model","anchor_text":"via the Stackelberg game in the payment rule. Furthermore, on the one hand the work here complements","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"By exploiting auction rules including the determination rule, payment rule, and allocation rule the interaction between the SFCs and RUs is greatly simplified. For instance, the determination rule can easily identify the number of RUs that are participating in the auction process, which further leverage the determination of the auction price via the Stackelberg game in the payment rule.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"By exploiting auction rules including the determination rule, payment rule, and allocation rule the interaction between the SFCs and RUs is greatly simplified. For instance, the determination rule can easily identify the number of RUs that are participating in the auction process, which further leverage the determination of the auction price via the Stackelberg game in the payment rule."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"no on Fig. 3. Determination of the Vickrey price, the maximum auction price, and To the number of pa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"ual fashion where each time slot has a suitable time duration based on the type of application, e.g.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as pmint hereinafter. ed However, we note that this secon","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price p_t^{max} for the participating J −1 RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as p_t^{min} hereinafter. However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if p_t is set to p_t = p_t^{max}, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between p_t^{max} and p_t^{min}.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price p_t^{max} for the participating J −1 RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as p_t^{min} hereinafter. However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if p_t is set to p_t = p_t^{max}, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between p_t^{max} and p_t^{min}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"a lower net beneﬁt. Hence, Ui can be seen as a net beneﬁt ne to RU i for sharing its ES. The utility","equation_id":"(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"pt −ri x∗i = . (11) 2αi 7 Now, substituting the value of x∗i into (8) and performing some 8 simple a","equation_id":"(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["response_based_bounded_auction_pricing"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L6-6ef68b2840","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"response_based_bounded_auction_pricing"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"70bc095c02578bf031b0d54ba69d5113bf40e26156d0d083a18baa255d2a6d9d"},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. | Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1. | Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. | Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. | Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g04-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"39afd20ea0ea72205a9a8a085e4da4716b0ead9015ac1c00c330d489bd6248a9"},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The auction price is the price SFC customers must pay RU owners for sharing their ES devices. Scope: The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"5419cc826592f82522f0bb04ae5e378cdd735affdcb7cd0978f11399b95e55e0"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. State-of-the-Art","anchor_text":"ge revenues for stakeholders [28], [29]. However, one similar- or- ity among most of the above menti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"the proposed modiﬁed auction scheme studied in Section IV 0) can be adopted in each time slot t = 1,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each participating RU i, the ES amount x_i chosen in response to the announced price p_t lies in [0, b_i] and maximizes U_i(x_i) = (p_t - r_i)x_i - α_i x_i^2; equivalently, x_i^* is the argmax of that utility over 0 ≤ x_i ≤ b_i. Scope: Stackelberg price-signal coordination for participating RUs in the community ES-sharing auction; the time-varying extension applies the same per-slot response.","expression":"x_i^* = \\arg\\max_{0 \\le x_i \\le b_i} \\left[(p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2\\right]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R003-x-x_i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i","v141-c-R003-theta-b_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The auctioneer's announced price p_t is restricted to the interval [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], where p_t^{min} is the Vickrey price (second-highest reservation price) and p_t^{max} the highest reservation price for participating RUs. Scope: Stackelberg payment-rule price strategy in the community ES-sharing auction.","expression":"p_t \\in [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min","v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g01-E35"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Equation (11) reports the RU best response for a given price p_t as x_i^* = (p_t - r_i)/(2α_i). Scope: RU best response in the Stackelberg payment rule; the bounded argmax in C002 retains the source's [0, b_i] constraint.","expression":"x_i^* = \\frac{p_t - r_i}{2\\alpha_i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R003-x-x_i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E11"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E14"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"er- nality properties, as we will see later, which are desirable in he any mechanism that adopts auc","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, the proposed auction process, as shown in Fig. 2, consists of three elements: 1) Owner: The RUs in set $\\mathcal{N}$, which own the ES devices, and expect to earn some economic benefits, e.g., through maximizing a utility function, by letting the SFCs to share some fraction of their ES spaces. 2) Customer: The SFCs in set $\\mathcal{M}$, which are in need of ESs in order to store some excess electricity at a particular time of the day. The SFCs offer the RUs a price with a view to jointly owning some fraction of their ES devices. 3) Auctioneer: A third party (e.g., estate or building manager), which controls the auction process between the owners and the customers according to some predefined rules."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E36","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as pmint hereinafter. ed However, we note that this secon","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if $p_t$ is set to $p_t = p_t^{\\max}$, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between $p_t^{\\max}$ and $p_t^{\\min}$. To do so, we propose a scheme for deciding on both the auction price $p_t$ and the amount of ESs $x_i$ that RUs will put into the market for sharing according to $p_t$. In particular, we propose a Stackelberg game between the auctioneer, which decides on the auction price $p_t$ to maximize the average cost savings to the SFCs as well as satisfying their desirable needs of ESs, and the RUs, which decide on the vector containing the amounts of ES $\\mathbf{x} = [x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{J-1}]$ that they would like to put into the market for sharing such that their benefits are maximized."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g04-e07","v141-b-g02-E15"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p12-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Case Study","anchor_text":"p gy y his have enough ES to share with the SFC. However, the ES to ed share in time slot 4 stems fr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. System Model","anchor_text":"via the Stackelberg game in the payment rule. Furthermore, on the one hand the work here complements","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"By exploiting auction rules including the determination rule, payment rule, and allocation rule the interaction between the SFCs and RUs is greatly simplified. For instance, the determination rule can easily identify the number of RUs that are participating in the auction process, which further leverage the determination of the auction price via the Stackelberg game in the payment rule."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E26"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"no on Fig. 3. Determination of the Vickrey price, the maximum auction price, and To the number of pa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"ual fashion where each time slot has a suitable time duration based on the type of application, e.g.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","expression":"p_t \\in [p_t^{\\min}, p_t^{\\max}]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-pmin","v141-c-R005-th-pmax"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E09"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as pmint hereinafter. ed However, we note that this secon","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price p_t^{max} for the participating J −1 RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as p_t^{min} hereinafter. However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if p_t is set to p_t = p_t^{max}, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between p_t^{max} and p_t^{min}."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The auctioneer's average cost savings objective per SFC is Z = ((Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m − p_t))/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i, and the auctioneer chooses p_t to maximize Z over [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}].","expression":"Z = \\left( \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K-1}(a_m - p_t)}{K-1} \\right) \\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i, \\quad p_t \\in [p_t^{\\min}, p_t^{\\max}]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p","v141-c-R005-x-xi"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-a","v141-c-R005-th-K","v141-c-R005-th-J","v141-c-R005-th-pmin","v141-c-R005-th-pmax"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g01-E36"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E36","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as pmint hereinafter. ed However, we note that this secon","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, we note that this second highest price might not be considerably beneficial for all the participating RUs in the auction scheme. In contrast, if $p_t$ is set to $p_t = p_t^{\\max}$, the price could be detrimental for some of the SFCs. Therefore, to make the auction scheme attractive and beneficial to all the participating RUs and, at the same time, to be cost effective for all the SFCs, we strike a balance between $p_t^{\\max}$ and $p_t^{\\min}$. To do so, we propose a scheme for deciding on both the auction price $p_t$ and the amount of ESs $x_i$ that RUs will put into the market for sharing according to $p_t$. In particular, we propose a Stackelberg game between the auctioneer, which decides on the auction price $p_t$ to maximize the average cost savings to the SFCs as well as satisfying their desirable needs of ESs, and the RUs, which decide on the vector containing the amounts of ES $\\mathbf{x} = [x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_{J-1}]$ that they would like to put into the market for sharing such that their benefits are maximized."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For a given auction price p_t, each participating RU i maximizes U_i(x_i) = (p_t − r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2 over 0 ≤ x_i ≤ b_i; the unique best response is x_i^*(p_t) = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i).","expression":"\\forall i \\in \\{1,\\ldots,J-1\\}: \\quad U_i(x_i) = (p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2, \\quad 0 \\le x_i \\le b_i; \\quad x_i^*(p_t) = \\arg\\max_{0 \\le x_i \\le b_i} \\left[ (p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2 \\right] = \\frac{p_t - r_i}{2\\alpha_i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p","v141-c-R005-x-xi"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-r","v141-c-R005-th-alpha","v141-c-R005-th-b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"a lower net beneﬁt. Hence, Ui can be seen as a net beneﬁt ne to RU i for sharing its ES. The utility","equation_id":"(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Substituting the RU best response into Z yields the unique auction price p_t^* that maximizes average SFC cost savings, given by equation (12).","expression":"p_t^* = \\frac{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{1}{2\\alpha_i}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} a_m\\right) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{r_i(K-1)}{2\\alpha_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{K-1}{\\alpha_i}}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-a","v141-c-R005-th-r","v141-c-R005-th-alpha","v141-c-R005-th-K","v141-c-R005-th-J"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E15"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"pt −ri x∗i = . (11) 2αi 7 Now, substituting the value of x∗i into (8) and performing some 8 simple a","equation_id":"(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auction price is the price SFC customers must pay RU owners for sharing their ES devices. Scope: The proposed modified auction for joint ES ownership between RUs and SFCs in the smart community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x-p_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The auctioneer chooses the auction price p_t, which is the price SFCs pay RU owners for shared ES, from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}].","expression":"p_t \\in [p_t^{\\min}, p_t^{\\max}]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x-p_t"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-theta-pmin","v141-c-R006-theta-pmax"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g01-E35"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"ED APPROACH 1467 its In the proposed approach, each RU i iteratively responds to the to strategy pt ","equation_id":"(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, the aim of the auctioneer is assumed to be to maximize the average cost savings Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i (8) by choosing an appropriate price p_t to offer to each RU from the range [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]. Here, Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1) is the average saving in auction price that the SFCs pay to the RUs for sharing the ESs and Σ_i x_i is the total amount of ES that all the SFCs share from the RUs. From Z, we note that the cost savings will be more if p_t is lower for all m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1}. However, this is offset by that fact that a lower p_t may lead to the choice of lower x_i ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} by the RUs, which in turn will affect the cost to the SFCs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-p_t","symbol":"p_t","meaning":"Auction price announced by the auctioneer as the price signal for sharing ES, per unit of energy in the source's Stackelberg payment rule.","kind":"operational","domain":"[p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g01-E36"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-p_t"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-x_i","symbol":"x_i","meaning":"Amount or fraction of ES space that RU i chooses to share in response to the announced auction price p_t.","kind":"operational","domain":"[0, b_i]","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g01-E12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-x_i"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-p","symbol":"p_t","meaning":"Auction price chosen by the auctioneer and paid by SFCs to RUs per unit of shared ES.","kind":"operational","domain":"[p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-p"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-xi","symbol":"x_i","meaning":"Amount or fraction of ES space that RU i offers to share with SFCs in response to the auction price.","kind":"operational","domain":"[0, b_i]","unit":"energy (ES space; source uses ES space and energy interchangeably)","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x-p_t","symbol":"p_t","meaning":"Auction price per unit of shared ES chosen by the auctioneer and paid by SFC customers to RU owners for sharing ES devices.","kind":"operational","domain":"[p_t^{\\min}, p_t^{\\max}]","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-p_t"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","symbol":"r_i","meaning":"Reservation price per unit of energy set by RU i; a fixed input to the RU's best response to the announced price p_t in this coordination stage.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"r_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-r_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i","symbol":"α_i","meaning":"Reluctance parameter of RU i measuring its unwillingness to share ES; a fixed coefficient in the RU utility used in the best response.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"α_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-b_i","symbol":"b_i","meaning":"Maximum shareable ES space of RU i, defined in the source as s_i^{cap} - d_i; it is the upper bound of the RU's ES-sharing strategy.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"s_i^{cap} - d_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E17"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-b_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min","symbol":"p_t^{min}","meaning":"Lower bound on the auctioneer's price signal; identified in the source as the Vickrey price or second-highest reservation price for the participating RUs.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_t^{min} (Vickrey price)"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max","symbol":"p_t^{max}","meaning":"Upper bound on the auctioneer's price signal; identified in the source as the highest reservation price among the participating RUs at the supply-demand intersection.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_t^{max}"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-a","symbol":"a_m","meaning":"Reservation bid of SFC m: the maximum per-unit price SFC m is willing to pay for sharing ES with RUs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-a"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-r","symbol":"r_i","meaning":"Reservation price of RU i per unit of energy.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-r"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-alpha","symbol":"\\alpha_i","meaning":"Reluctance parameter of RU i measuring its unwillingness to share ES.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-alpha"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-b","symbol":"b_i","meaning":"Maximum amount of battery/ES space that RU i can share, defined in the source as b_i = s_i^{cap} - d_i.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"energy (ES space)","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-b"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-K","symbol":"K","meaning":"Number of participating SFCs determined by the determination/matching rule; the pricing sums use K-1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-K"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-J","symbol":"J","meaning":"Number of participating RUs determined by the determination/matching rule; the pricing sums use J-1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-J"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-pmin","symbol":"p_t^{min}","meaning":"Vickrey price: the second-highest reservation price among the participating J-1 RUs, serving as the lower bound of the auction-price strategy.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-pmin"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-pmax","symbol":"p_t^{max}","meaning":"Highest reservation price for the participating J-1 RUs at the supply-demand intersection, serving as the upper bound of the auction-price strategy.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-pmax"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta-pmin","symbol":"p_t^{\\min}","meaning":"Lower bound of the allowed auction price: the Vickrey price, i.e., the second-highest reservation price among the participating J−1 RUs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-pmin"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-theta-pmax","symbol":"p_t^{\\max}","meaning":"Upper bound of the allowed auction price: the highest reservation price for the participating J−1 RUs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-pmax"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"response_based_bounded_auction_pricing","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The auctioneer, incorporating the RU supply response, selects and publishes the unit shared energy storage price p_t within [p_t^min,p_t^max] to maximize the SFC average cost saving Z=[Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m−p_t)/(K−1)]Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the unit auction price of the shared resource","Core operation: incorporating the autonomous supply response, maximize the buyers' average cost saving within the allowed interval","Output: the auction price p_t used for demand response and payments"],"variation_fields":["p_t^min is what the source calls the Vickrey price, namely the second-highest reserve price among the RU participants; p_t^max is its highest reserve price","Equation (12) reports p_t^*=[(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}1/(2α_i))(Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}a_m)+Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}r_i(K−1)/(2α_i)]/[Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}(K−1)/α_i]","Algorithm 1 searches over the price interval, uses the RU bounded best response to calculate Z, and records the price when Z≥Z*; it is retained separately from equation (12)","Final pricing in the payment rule is executed after the group is determined; the earlier determination of the price upper bound and the time-slot-by-time-slot implementation scope are retained"],"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001"],"paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/228"});
